ProsperoSunshine: quitting while another device streams ends only the quitting device's stream

With a second player, /cancel from either device ended every session and the app, and with close_game_on_quit also the
game the others were playing. While a session of another client runs, /cancel now ends only the sessions (and the kept
gamepads) of the client that sent it. The last client to quit ends the app as before.

--- a/src/nvhttp.cpp
+++ b/src/nvhttp.cpp
@@ -1651,6 +1651,16 @@
     tree.put("root.cancel", 1);
     tree.put("root.<xmlattr>.status_code", 200);
 
+#ifdef __SCE__
+    // A second player: while another device streams, quitting ends only this device's stream, so the app and the game
+    // stay for the others. The last one to quit ends the app as before.
+    if (!last_verified_client_cert.empty() && rtsp_stream::session_count_except_cert(last_verified_client_cert) > 0) {
+      BOOST_LOG(info) << "Quit from one device while another streams: ending only its stream"sv;
+      rtsp_stream::terminate_sessions_by_cert(last_verified_client_cert);
+      return;
+    }
+#endif
+
     rtsp_stream::terminate_sessions();
 
     if (proc::proc.running() > 0) {
